  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Investment Promotion and Access to Finance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Kosovo):  This activity works to strengthen private sector capacity for sustainable economic growth through investment promotion and increased access to diversified finance. Expanding sources of investment and finance will enable the private sector to grow, create productive jobs, increase exports, and adopt new technologies and business practices. By doing so, this activity contributes to USAID&apos;s overall goal of increasing opportunities for inclusive democratic and economic participation and aligns with ICS Objective 3.1, while broadly supporting Kosovo&apos;s readiness for EU accession, contributing to ICS Objective 1.3. The activity will include support to relevant GoK institutions, including the Office of the Prime Minister, Ministry of Finance, Central Bank of Kosovo, and others to strengthen their capacities to attract investment and increase access to diversified finance. The activity will support Kosovo&apos;s new Investment Promotion Agency, housed in the Office of the Prime Minister, through development of a legal framework that supports investment attraction. The activity will partner with private sector entities to attract investment flows and set up investment funds in Kosovo. It will develop the legal and regulatory framework for introducing capital markets in Kosovo, and support the growth of alternative financing products, such as crowdfunding and accounts receivable financing, as well as supporting private sector businesses on investment readiness.  The activity aligns with CAATSA Goal 8 supporting economic resilience (20% of funding) through technical assistance in promoting investment and increasing diversified finance.  The activity aligns with JRS Goal 2.2 to strengthen democratic systems, institutions, and processes....</narrative>
  </description>
